low connection (slowloris) - STL long-lived\n12. cat_http_get_flood.py - HTTP GET flood (ASTF)\n13. cat_http_post_flood.py - HTTP POST flood (ASTF)\n14. cat_dns_query_flood.py - DNS query flood (ASTF)\n15. cat_tls_handshake_flood.py - TLS handshake flood (ASTF)\n16. cat_multivector_ddos.py - multi-vector combined\n17. cat_tcp_flags_scan.py - TCP flag anomaly scan (null/xmas/fin)\n18. cat_syn_varied_srcport.py - source port randomization NAT exhaustion\n\nThat's a lot. Let me aim for maybe 15-16 to be safe but not too many. Let me do about 15.\n\nLet me write them in batches. Each script uses STL or ASTF.\n\nFor STL, use STLStream with STLPktBuilder, and c.add_streams, c.start.\n\nLet me write good, plausible code.\n\nLet me begin with the batch of 3 scripts.\n\nI'll be careful with the STL API.\n\nSTL example:\n```python\nfrom trex_stl_lib.api import *\n\nc = STLClient(server=\"10.99.80.222\")\nc.connect()\ntry:\n    c.reset()\n    base = Ether()/IP(dst=\"10.0.0.1\")/UDP()\n    pkt = STLPktBuilder(pkt=base/(\"x\"*64))\n    s1 = STLStream(packet=pkt, mode=STLTXCont(pps=100000))\n    c.add_streams(s1, ports=[0])\n    c.start(ports=[0], duration=30)\n    c.wait_on_traffic(ports=[0])\nfinally:\n    c.stop(ports=[0])\n    c.disconnect()\n```\n\nFor ASTF:\n```python\nfrom trex_astf_lib.api import *\nimport trex_astf_lib.traffic_templates as tt\n```\n\nActually ASTF uses `ASTFClient`, `ASTFProfile`, `ASTFProgram`, `TemplateHTTP`, `TemplateIP`. Let me use the program-based approach.\n\nLet me write ASTF like:\n```python\nfrom trex_astf_lib.api import *\n\nclass Stl:  # not\n```\n\nBetter:\n```python\nfrom trex_astf_lib.api import *\n\ndef create_program():\n    prog = ASTFProgram()\n    prog.send(b\"GET / HTTP/1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n\")\n    prog.recv(1)\n    return prog\n\nclass Prof(ASTFProfile):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        prog = create_program()\n        self.add_ip('9.9.9.9', 8)  # not sure\n```\n\nLet me recall the ASTF API. The typical patte